{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":583611,"name":null,"username":"zuohanwen1009","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/z/49beb7/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:45:48.725Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI've been building Cheetah, a local LLM loader/backend focused on extreme memory efficiency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter a full refactor, the numbers changed by an order of magnitude:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e0.5B model: 2GB+ → 62MB (idle)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e1.5B model: OOM → 67MB (idle)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIncremental memory for a 1.5B model over 0.5B: only +5MB\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e0.5B on an i5-4200M (2013): 13 tok/s (self-developed CPU backend with SIMD)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTool-call overhead (e.g. weather query): +0.2MB\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe goal isn't raw speed first — it's fitting usable local models into embedded/low-VRAM environments. The memory numbers come from a lazy-loading architecture and a self-developed CPU/Vulkan backend (CUDA/Metal currently via Candle as a transition).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStill early (V1 offload has ~0.5GB runtime overhead, being replaced in V2 by VRAM→RAM→DISK tiering for MoE). README has the full architecture, memory-loading internals, and contribution guide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepo: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/DA3M0/cheetah\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - DA3M0/Cheetah: A single-binary local LLM inference server in Rust + C. Supports Safetensors (F32/F16/BF16) CPU/CUDA/Metal/Vulkan. OpenAI-compatible gateway · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHappy to answer questions about the memory model or the CPU backend.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-15T13:45:48.725Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":22,"reads":72,"readers_count":71,"score":139.4,"yo